[test-suite name=did ring=2
  [doc [#
conformance fixtures for cx-stdlib/did (spec/03-approved/std-lib/did.md).
Authored at the I3 open (partition corpus audit gap G14): did.md previously
had V-tests only; these fixtures pin the module surface itself. Ring 2 by
the partition plan-row contract (did/vc underpin the Ring-2 single
authority model, cx_partition.md §11) even though every fixtured lane here
is pure/offline — see the I3 ledger census note N3.

   DETERMINISM: keys are fixed literals, never generated. Golden material
   (the same convention as vcx/tests/stdlib_did_test.v):
     seed-1 = 0102…1f20 (bytes 1..32)
       pub-1  = 79b5562e8fe654f94078b112e8a98ba7901f853ae695bed7e0e3910bad049664
       did-1  = did:key:z6MkneMkZqwqRiU5mJzSG3kDwzt9P8C59N4NGTfBLfSGE7c7
     seed-2 = 4041…5e5f (bytes 0x40..0x5f)
       pub-2  = 2543b92ff1095511476adc8369db6ddc933665a11978dda1404ee1066ca9559d
       did-2  = did:key:z6Mkgxj2R3HLtQRpPnvfvpuKEceSqf3tZHBjdmZ3fFz3JHGG
   ed25519-sign is deterministic, so signatures over fixed challenges pin.
   Every case is offline (the air-gapped did:key/did:peer:0 posture, §6);
   the ONE network-touching surface (resolve of did:web) is fixtured at its
   capability-DENIAL lane only — no fixture grants net. Case 023 carries an
   explicit grant="read": the denial arrives as an [err …] VALUE (rc=0), so
   the harness three-way policy (which scans out-err for CXER0271) would
   otherwise default to grant-all and the case would hit the live network.

   SPEC-FINDINGS pinned as shipped (fixture-before-fix):
   - document/key-of on a non-self-describing method reports
     CXER-DID-NOT-SELF-DESCRIBING even for methods outside the §2 v1 set
     (did:ion) — CXER-DID-METHOD-UNSUPPORTED fires only at resolve
     (cases 014/022 pin both sides of that split).
   - resolve of did:web under a net denial surfaces the CXER0271 denial
     ITSELF (case 023). It used to arrive WRAPPED in a
     CXER-DID-DOC-MISMATCH `message=panic` envelope, which claimed a
     document-id mismatch when no document had been fetched at all and
     buried the real cause. Fixed by #740: reaching the document and the
     document being wrong about itself are different failures, so a fetch
     that fails with its own typed err propagates that err unchanged, a
     non-2xx / no-response becomes CXER-DID-RESOLVE-FAILED, and
     CXER-DID-DOC-MISMATCH is reserved for a fetched document that
     disagrees with its own DID.

   Id ranges:
     001-003  key-create (+ peer-create) construction + bad-length
     004-008  parse (key/web/peer) + malformed negatives
     009-010  method
     011-014  document: did:key full shape, did:peer id, not-self-describing
     015-017  key-of: round-trip, peer, non-Ed25519 multicodec
     018-020  verify-control: pass, wrong signer, stale challenge
     021-023  resolve: offline did:key, unsupported method, did:web denial
     024-025  peer-create golden + key-of on did:web
#]]

 [case id=did-001-key-create-golden level=core gate=enforced
  [tags did key-create multibase]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/did']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/bytes']
[$did:key-create [$bytes:from-hex "79b5562e8fe654f94078b112e8a98ba7901f853ae695bed7e0e3910bad049664"]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
'did:key:z6MkneMkZqwqRiU5mJzSG3kDwzt9P8C59N4NGTfBLfSGE7c7'
#]]
 ]

 [case id=did-002-key-create-second-key level=core gate=enforced
  [tags did key-create determinism]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/did']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/bytes']
[$did:key-create [$bytes:from-hex "2543b92ff1095511476adc8369db6ddc933665a11978dda1404ee1066ca9559d"]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
'did:key:z6Mkgxj2R3HLtQRpPnvfvpuKEceSqf3tZHBjdmZ3fFz3JHGG'
#]]
 ]

 [case id=did-003-key-create-bad-length level=core gate=enforced
  [tags did key-create negative key-length]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/did']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/bytes']
[$did:key-create [$bytes:from-hex "0102030405"]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[err code=cx-err:CXER-DID-KEY-UNSUPPORTED message='did/key-create: Ed25519 public key must be 32 bytes, got 5']
#]]
 ]

 [case id=did-004-parse-did-key level=core gate=enforced
  [tags did parse structural]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/did']
[$did:parse "did:key:z6MkneMkZqwqRiU5mJzSG3kDwzt9P8C59N4NGTfBLfSGE7c7"]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[did method=key id=z6MkneMkZqwqRiU5mJzSG3kDwzt9P8C59N4NGTfBLfSGE7c7 raw=did:key:z6MkneMkZqwqRiU5mJzSG3kDwzt9P8C59N4NGTfBLfSGE7c7]
#]]
 ]

